# Run data, never source. Journal rotation archives (and any journal
# fragment directory) must never reach the index: one archived run is
# hundreds of per-core files, and an unignored archive folder shows up in
# a commit as "675 files changed". These patterns cover journals under
# any -log name, not just the default cpu-stability.log.
journal-archive-*/
*.journal.jsonl
*.journal.jsonl.workers/

# scripts/gate.ps1 writes its log next to the run by default; gate logs
# are evidence and belong in the operator's log directory, not the tree.
gate-*.log
# Per-machine configuration. `config init` writes it, it carries this
# machine's external-tool paths, and it is deliberately not versioned:
# a checked-in config would be someone else's machine.
config.json

# Per-machine configuration. `config init` writes it, it carries this
# machine's external-tool paths, and it is deliberately not versioned:
# a checked-in config would be someone else's machine.
config.json
